[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue, "dates parse mm/dd in eu locales". Read
report by report, it holds three different problems. Only the first is the one the fix queue
is aimed at.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one known bug. Fixing the parser will not fix problems 2 and 3.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemSplit ticket={4471} />

## 1 · The shared parser reads dates month first

Day-first tenants (en-GB, nl-NL, cs-CZ, fr-FR, it-IT, pl-PL, da-DK, en-IE, and the rest through
the app, email and booking-v2 forms) see day and month swapped: "booked 2 December, invite says
12 February". This is what #4471 was filed for.

## 2 · booking-v3 form prints the wrong hint

Tenants on booking-v3 with a day-first locale (copper.studio, alder.physio, pale.harbour) type
what the hint under the date field tells them: month first. The form then reads it day first.
The parser is not at fault; the hint is. A parser fix leaves these reports open. It affects the
form channel only.

## 3 · Bookings one day off

A small group of reports are not a day/month swap: the date is one day off ("every booking in June is
one day off", "the invite arrived before I made the booking", Lisbon and Toronto getting
different days for one meeting). That is a timezone or day-boundary problem. By tenant locale
the desk filed them under problem 1; the desk's own note
(`desk-notes.json`, `oneDayMove`) lists them: R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620.

## Why the merge hid this

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line. Intake tags are a
guess from the reporter's browser and disagree with the real cause for dozens of reports. Merge
on cause (tenant locale, booking form, channel), not subject; see
[triage](/kb/triage/dedupe).

